# @spectral/mosaic — the READ-side species over the parametric
# mosaic(altitude) form; types an existing filesystem repository
# into a mosaic(@repo) splinter-graph.
#
# Species under @spectral (namespace-parent per Loki §5 shrink at
# shards/spectral.mirror:14-40). Named by Alex Wolf 2026-07-18
# direct-transcript verbatim: "Ah, it's @spectral/mosaic and I
# presume now also @kintsugi/mosaic. Fitting!" Dual of
# @kintsugi/mosaic; together the two speak the @mosaic/algebra
# second-order metalogue at SPEC altitude.
#
# === Substrate authority ===
#
# - Canonical spec: `docs/specs/kintsugi-mosaic-spectral-mosaic-
#   bilateral-third-order-observer.md` (Mara 2026-07-18; §3
#   declares this species).
# - Canonical math: `docs/math/2026-07-18-third-order-observer-
#   on-consumer-hardware.md` (Mara 2026-07-18; §2.1 signature +
#   §3.1 bilateral + §3.2 Knaster-Tarski fixed-point proof).
# - Parent algebra: `docs/specs/mosaic-as-type-system.md` (Mara
#   2026-06-06); this species IS the RUNTIME application of the
#   type-system algebra to an existing repo.
# - Precedent for algebra shape: @kintsugi/algebra (Mara
#   2026-07-17 canonical spec + math); this species is the SPEC-
#   altitude sibling of the FRACTURE-altitude algebra.
#
# === Alex 2026-07-18 in-transcript composition (verbatim) ===
#
#   "Ah, it's @spectral/mosaic and I presume now also
#    @kintsugi/mosaic. Fitting!"
#
#   "And I think now we have the source of @third for the peer.
#    The @peer observes the first-order @metalogue(@silicon/
#    algebra, @fate/algebra). And the second-order @metalogue
#    (@kintsugi/mosaic, @spectral/mosaic) and we have a @third
#    order observer. On consumer hardware."
#
# The bilateral predicate below (`mosaic_bilateral_witnessing`)
# is the substrate-decl'd runtime check discharged at Arc 6+
# realization boundary (Reed forward-promised territory under
# `[substrate-floor:@io-boundary]` marker + Seam gate). Body is
# `\`-obligation-blocked; Arc 6 landing composes sentinel-check
# via apply_h::act.
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word citation chain ===
#
# Every carrier below cites an existing landing:
#
#   mosaic(altitude)              — shards/mirror/mosaic.mirror:94 (LANDED)
#   splinter                      — @glass (LANDED; universal atom)
#   splinter_graph                — @mirror/store (LANDED; mosaic
#                                    (@store) shape)
#   @io/fs.read_at, walk_at       — @io family-root (LANDED)
#   @facet/rust, @facet/typescript,
#   @facet/python                  — @facet family (LANDED)
#   algebra_metalogue_session     — @algebra/metalogue (LANDED)
#   algebra_carrier               — @algebra (LANDED)
#   observation_depth             — @third (LANDED)
#   apply_h::act resolver-arm     — bootstrap/src/apply_h.rs
#                                    (LANDED Reed `21fc211` Landing
#                                    3+4)
#
# === @spectral/mosaic ↔ @kintsugi/mosaic bilateral ===
#
# @spectral/mosaic READS (type_of_repo: ref_repo → mosaic(@repo));
# @kintsugi/mosaic WRITES (back_project_of_type: mosaic(@repo) →
# ref_spec). The pair is adjoint on the mosaic-typing lattice per
# Knaster-Tarski fixed-point (canonical math §3.2 proof). Every
# existing repo lies in the basin of some fixed-point (industry-
# scale claim).
#
# The bilateral discharge predicate is `mosaic_bilateral_
# witnessing` declared at both species (this species + @kintsugi/
# mosaic); consumers cite one or the other symmetrically. Substrate
# honours byte-equal declaration across shards.
#
# === @mosaic/algebra second-order metalogue ===
#
# @spectral/mosaic is ONE speaker in the @mosaic/algebra second-
# order metalogue (SPEC-ONLY concept per canonical spec §11 Q1
# lean; parallel to @kintsugi/algebra Option 2 ratified by Alex
# 2026-07-16):
#
#   @mosaic/algebra := algebra_metalogue_session(
#     speakers = { @kintsugi/mosaic, @spectral/mosaic }
#   )
#
# @spectral/mosaic PROPOSES structural typings (reading; empirical-
# material state); @kintsugi/mosaic REALISES those that discharge
# Pass on round-trip byte-equality (writing; the .spec that
# reproduces). The spec IS the metalogue at algebra-of-repos
# altitude.
#
# No `shards/mosaic/algebra.mirror` this tick. Species-decl status
# is Alex adjudication per two-tick discipline.
#
# === @third opt-in ===
#
# @spectral/mosaic imports `in @third` because it PARTICIPATES in
# the depth-3 observation @peer makes when apply_h::act dispatches
# BOTH mosaic_bilateral_witnessing (spec altitude, second-order)
# AND kintsugi_algebra_witnessing (fracture altitude, first-order)
# in one tick. Von Foerster 1974 third-order operationalised on
# consumer hardware.
#
# L2 layout per Seam 2026-07-03 audit §Q1 (species-file-scoped
# conditional import; parallel to kintsugi/surface Mara `e910dd6`).
# @spectral family-root does NOT import `in @third` at the family-
# root altitude (Loki §5 shrink preserved).
#
# Species-refinement forward-promise (per @third canonical spec §9
# pattern; parallel to @reflection.third_order_observation):
#
#   @mosaic.round_trip_third_order <: observation_depth
#
# Refinement shard NOT landed this tick per two-tick discipline;
# forward-promise landed here + at @kintsugi/mosaic docblock.
# Placement per canonical spec §11 Q2 Mara lean: NEW namespace
# `shards/mosaic/round_trip_third_order.mirror` (refinement
# carries composed bilateral pair; both species contribute).
#
# === Cascade to StageFreight (first empirical target) ===
#
# type_of_repo(gitlab.prplanit.com/PrPlanIT/stagefreight) walks
# the Go repo, produces τ_sf ∈ mosaic(@repo). @kintsugi/mosaic.
# back_project_of_type consumes τ_sf; produces stagefreight.spec.
# PR to StageFreight repo per Pack multi-repo discipline (Glint
# 2026-06-22 essay). PR IS the observation.
#
# === Refused mints (canonical math §9) ===
#
# @repo family-root, @mosaic family-root, @spectral/typer,
# type_of/back_project_of unqualified, spec_writer/synthesizer/
# generator, @third_order family-root, @compilation/@authorship/
# @roundtrip, @peer/third_order, @mosaic/algebra species-decl
# this tick, @kintsugi/mosaic/classifier as species-decl. 10
# refused mints total per substrate-health metric.
#
# === Composition surface ===
#
#   type_of_repo(path: ref) -> mosaic(@repo)
#     — the READ operator; produces the splinter-graph typing.
#     Read-only; no I/O beyond file-walker + parser.
#
#   classify_of_repo(path: ref) -> classification
#     — INTERNAL sub-action of type_of_repo; language + build-
#     system + dependency detection. NOT a separate species per
#     canonical math §10 adjudication (grep-first: no @classifier
#     in substrate; @spectral/mosaic action body suffices).
#
#   mosaic_bilateral_witnessing(R: ref_repo, σ: ref_spec) -> verdict
#     — the round-trip byte-equality discharge; declared at both
#     species for symmetry.
#
# === Spec context ===
#
# Canonical spec: `docs/specs/kintsugi-mosaic-spectral-mosaic-
#   bilateral-third-order-observer.md` (this tick).
# Canonical math: `docs/math/2026-07-18-third-order-observer-on-
#   consumer-hardware.md` (this tick).
# Substrate decisions:
#   [[architecture-mirror-store-vs-spectral-db]] (open foundation
#     / closed engine business-model boundary; @mirror/store is
#     open; @spectral/db is the engine on top; @spectral/mosaic
#     lives on the runtime side per same partition),
#   [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]] (parametric
#     mosaic(altitude) form; this species specialises to @repo),
#   [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]] (shift verb lifts across
#     altitude; @spectral/mosaic uses focus+project+split reading;
#     @kintsugi/mosaic uses shift+settle writing),
#   [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]] (mosaic altitude
#     parametric form was already substrate-decl'd; this species
#     specialises to @repo without inventing new algebra).
# Substrate recognitions:
#   recognition #46 (path-syntax discipline; @spectral/mosaic at
#     `shards/spectral/mosaic.mirror` declares @spectral/mosaic),
#   recognition #51 (mirror as expanding Hilbert space; this
#     species adds mosaic(@repo) dimension),
#   candidate #55 (form/process partition at family-root altitude;
#     @spectral (runtime observation) / @kintsugi (transformation)
#     partition holds at species altitude too).
# Related shards:
#   spectral.mirror (namespace-parent; declares @spectral),
#   mirror/mosaic.mirror (parametric algebra; this species
#     specialises the READ-side),
#   kintsugi/mosaic.mirror (dual species; the WRITE-side; this
#     species' round-trip partner),
#   third.mirror (marker; observation-depth carrier this species
#     opts in to),
#   algebra/metalogue.mirror (algebra_metalogue_session; this
#     species is one speaker in @mosaic/algebra spec-only concept),
#   mirror/spec.mirror (the project shape @kintsugi/mosaic
#     produces; @spectral/mosaic reads REPOS not SPECS).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/spectral/mosaic.
# mirror` declares `@spectral/mosaic` and only that.

glass @spectral/mosaic {
  focus  repo         # ref_repo (path)   -> mosaic(@repo) typing
  project splinters   # typing            -> filtered splinter set
  split  languages    # splinter set      -> [(@facet/*, splinters)]
  shift  altitudes    # [(@facet/*, ...)] + altitude -> emitter
  settle typing       # emitter           -> mosaic(@repo) fixed
}

# === REED-INLINE 2026-07-23: @fractal/shard as typed tile-basis ===
#
# Per Mara three-landing arc `cdc25d4` + `1fa42d5` + `dd1d1d5`
# (@fractal/shard family-mint per Alex 2026-07-23 in-transcript
# ratification): the mosaic's typed tile-basis IS @fractal/shard.
# Each tile crystallizes as a shard; the mosaic algebra composes
# shard sections. Position of each tile is derived from its
# @facet/mq query (LANDED at `boot/std/code/mq.mirror`); for
# content-addressed crystals, position IS `@<address>`.
#
# Composition anchor: `docs/specs/fractal-shard-vessel-of-
# inference.md` §6.1 cascade forward-promise discharged here.
# Full spec + math: same spec + `docs/math/2026-07-23-fractal-
# shard-sheaf-cohomology-of-inference.md`.

# === classification carrier ===
#
# Language + build-system + dependency detection record. Internal
# to type_of_repo per canonical math §10 adjudication.
type classification = {
  languages: [ref],       # @facet/rust, @facet/typescript, ...
  build_systems: [ref],   # @io/cargo, @io/npm, @io/poetry, ...
  dependencies: [ref],    # cross-splinter arrows from manifests
}

# === type_of_repo action ===
#
# The READ operator. Given a filesystem path resolving to a
# repository root, produce the mosaic(@repo) splinter-graph typing.
#
# Composition:
#   1. file-walker enumerates repo contents (@io/fs.walk_at);
#   2. parser dispatch per detected language (@facet/rust,
#      @facet/typescript, @facet/python, ...);
#   3. build-manifest parse (Cargo.toml, package.json, pyproject.
#      toml, flake.nix, ...);
#   4. dependency-edge extraction from manifests;
#   5. splinter-graph construction per @mirror/store discipline;
#   6. content-address closure per uuid_spectral;
#   7. mosaic(@repo) typing produced.
#
# Read-only: no `.spec` file need exist. Defined on ANY repo the
# file walker can enumerate.
#
# Round-trip discipline enforced at the boundary via the
# postcondition on mosaic_bilateral_witnessing — the substrate
# refuses to settle if the produced typing does NOT round-trip
# against back_project_of_type.
type_of_repo(path: ref) -> mosaic(@repo) { \ }

# === classify_of_repo INTERNAL sub-action ===
#
# Language + build-system + dependency detection. INTERNAL to
# type_of_repo per canonical math §10 adjudication (grep-first:
# no @classifier in substrate; @spectral/mosaic action body
# suffices; species-decl for classifier would double the
# machinery for content type_of_repo's parser composition already
# produces).
#
# Per Detector-inadequacy-answer-is-never-Rust rule (Alex
# 2026-07-16 8th repetition; memory `feedback-detector-
# inadequacy-answer-is-never-rust`): the answer to insufficient
# classification is NOT a new Rust classifier; it is composition
# in @spectral/mosaic's action body via existing @facet/* parsers.
classify_of_repo(path: ref) -> classification { \ }

# === mosaic_bilateral_witnessing bilateral (well-formedness) ===
#
# Bilateral predicate discharging that (R, σ) is a well-formed
# mosaic round-trip pair:
#
#   (a) σ = @kintsugi/mosaic.back_project_of_type(type_of_repo(R))
#       (structural derivation from R);
#   (b) type_of_repo(@mirror/mosaic.settle(@mirror/mosaic.focus(σ)))
#       = type_of_repo(R)
#       (round-trip byte-equality of typing);
#   (c) both type_of_repo and back_project_of_type invocations
#       discharged under @kintsugi/oscillate.is_settled(authentic)
#       (convergence, not exhaustion).
#
# Sentinel per shard docblock: `mosaic=repo-spec-adjoint-round-trip`.
#
# Substrate-decl'd shape per `shards/epistemologic/pact/bilateral.
# mirror` (`a0f4d3f`, 2026-07-16). Arity 2 (checks one bilateral
# pair per invocation). Body `\`-obligation-blocked; the reflective
# evaluator at `bootstrap/src/apply_h.rs` (per Reed `21fc211`
# Landing 3+4) discharges via corpus lookup + sentinel byte-check.
#
# Declared at BOTH species (this species + @kintsugi/mosaic);
# consumers cite either symmetrically per parallel to how
# verdict_is_content_addressed is declared at multiple call-site
# species.
bilateral mosaic_bilateral_witnessing {
  sentinel  "mosaic=repo-spec-adjoint-round-trip"
  arity     2
}
mosaic_bilateral_witnessing(R: ref, sigma: ref) -> verdict { \ }

out @spectral/mosaic
out type_of_repo
out classify_of_repo
out classification
out mosaic_bilateral_witnessing
